WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.872
An application's secrets and certificates
each carry a start and an end date,

2
00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:09.770
in U T C, and those dates are enough to
test ScubaGear's three application rules:

3
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.592
no application passwords, passwords
valid for at most a hundred eighty days,

4
00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:18.725
and certificates valid for at most
three hundred sixty-five days.

5
00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:23.024
Microsoft's app management policies
enforce the same limits going forward;

6
00:00:23.024 --> 00:00:26.163
the check finds what existed
before they were turned on.

7
00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:30.795
Two related reads support consent review:
who has been given an application's roles,

8
00:00:30.795 --> 00:00:33.815
and which delegated permissions
have been consented,

9
00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:36.020
which needs Directory dot Read dot All.
